# .trivyignore — CVE / advisory suppressions for commercial-entitlements.
# Each entry must include an explanation and (where possible) an expiry date.
# Remove entries once the upstream fix is available and the image is re-pinned.
#
# Format: <CVE-or-advisory-ID> [exp:YYYY-MM-DD]
#         # comment explaining why it is suppressed and when to revisit

# DLA-4792-1: tzdata new timezone database (2026b → 2026c).
# This is a timezone data update, not a security vulnerability.
# gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot does not yet ship the fixed
# package version (tzdata 2026c-0+deb12u1); no patched distroless image is
# available upstream. Remove this entry once distroless ships tzdata 2026c.
DLA-4792-1

# DLA-4845-1: ca-certificates 20250419~deb12u1 → deb12u2.
# Removes distrusted Comodo "AAA Certificate Services" and "emSign ECC Root CA - G3" roots.
# Not exploitable: the Dockerfile's certs stage (debian:bookworm-slim, deb12u2) already
# replaces distroless's /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt. Trivy reports the finding
# only because it reads distroless's dpkg status metadata.
# Remove this entry and re-pin once distroless ships ca-certificates deb12u2.
DLA-4845-1 exp:2026-11-21

# DLA-4854-1: tzdata 2026b-0+deb12u1 → 2026e-0+deb12u1, timezone-database refresh.
# Not exploitable: the service never loads a zone (no time.LoadLocation, no
# time/tzdata, no time.Local use; all timestamps are UTC).
# Blocked upstream: distroless does not yet ship tzdata >= 2026e.
# Remove this entry and re-pin once distroless ships tzdata >= 2026e.
DLA-4854-1 exp:2026-11-30

# DLA-4867-1: tzdata 2026b → 2026f, same situation as DLA-4854-1 above.
DLA-4867-1 exp:2026-11-30

# GO-2026-5932: golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained and unsafe by design.
# Not exploitable: no package under cmd/, internal/ imports x/crypto/openpgp.
# The module arrives only via testcontainers-go (test dependency — not in production image).
# Remove this entry and bump x/crypto once a tagged release carries the fix.
GO-2026-5932 exp:2026-12-03
